<title>SPAIN: Spain July industrial production rose four percent.</title>
<headline>Spain July industrial production rose four percent.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Institute gave the following provisional figures (percentage change):</p>
<p> INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION		  JUL 96     JUN 96    JUL 95</p>
<p> Yr-yr					 4.0	 -5.7	 3.7</p>
<p> Avg yr to date against yr ago	-1.8	 -2.7	 7.3</p>
<p>The INE gave the following breakdown (percentage change):</p>
<p>					     JUL 96   JUN 96  YR-TO-DATE</p>
<p> Energy				    -0.9	-2.9	0.2</p>
<p> Non-energy minerals, chemicals     0.8	-5.6     -3.6</p>
<p> Metals, precision tools		5.0	-3.7	1.0</p>
<p> Other manufacturing		    7.4	-8.9     -3.9</p>
<p> Consumer goods			   8.1	-6.5     -2.0</p>
<p> Capital goods			    4.6	-1.4	1.6</p>
<p> Intermediary goods		     0.6	-6.4     -2.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Year-to-date column gives average increases.</p>
</text>
